  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Distance along a line i.e., displacement ( $s$ ) $=t^3\\left(\\because s \\propto t^3\\right.$ given $)$\nBy double differentiation of displacement, we get acceleration.\n$V=\\frac{d s}{d t}=\\frac{d t^3}{d t}=3 t^2$ and\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& a=\\frac{d v}{d t}=\\frac{d 3 t^2}{d t}=6 t \\\\\n& a=6 t \\text { or } a \\propto t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nHence graph (b) is correct.",
    "image": null
  },
